title: Syndicate election bribery
subtitle: Paying for drone absentions
priority: 5
max-visits: 1
tags: event
view-if: month = 12

The employment contracts of Megacorporation employees in Mikasa generally forbid them to vote for candidates the corporation deems unacceptable.  Consequently the ballots for corporate employees only ever have the name of the [+ corporate_party_name +] candidates approved by their employeers.  The only real choice is vote or abstain.  The Megacorps pay out some minor financial incentives to encourage voting but historically these have been small.

It seems that the syndiates have decided it's worth counter bribing the drones, paying them not to vote.  This would shift the electorate for general population elections in favor of the special interest parties who are more friendly to the syndicates.  The effect would be most strongly felt in the districts with the main corporate strongholds, the Railyard, Limelight and Vats.

-@useful
-@troubling

@useful
title: Fewer corporate votes is good for us
on-arrival: drone_syndicate_bribe_boost = 1; {! if (typeof Q.applySyndicateDroneMembershipBribe === 'function') { Q.applySyndicateDroneMembershipBribe() } !}
# TODO: replace direct IG.membership[] edit when ig_membership per-block overhaul lands (planning/ig_demographics.txt).

@troubling
title: Election bribery is epidemic
on-arrival: drone_corp_bribe_slip = 1